                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is one of those hidden gems on Steam, that is being buried under an avalanche of asset-flip crap and other low quality games.\nI like tactical games, and Steam Tactics did not disappoint me. The basic gameplay is rather simple: different guns have different attack patterns and damage types, you choose an optimal loadout for your ships, and the combat is basically about positioning: place your ships so you can deal maximum damage while avoiding or minimizing damage from counterattacks. This makes for a surprisingly deep and engaging gameplay. \n\n[b]Pros[/b]\n-Solid gameplay mechanics. Simple, yet clever and satisfying\n-Does not mentally overburden you. You have to think to win, but you can play in a pretty relaxed manner and don't have to calculate a ton of numbers for every turn and action you perform\n-Likeable characters\n-Visuals are nice. There is nothing really special about graphics here, but overall Steam Tactics looks very nice, and character art is very good\n-I liked the music, it is catchy and fits in the game pretty well\n-Steampunk! Why are there so few games in that setting?\n\n[b]Cons[/b]\n-The ending was not very spectacular, so I felt kinda disappointed\n-Music can get repetetive if you play long enough\n-$12 feels a bit overpriced? Though considering that you can spend quite a lot of time getting all achievements, that may not actually be the case\n\n[b]Arguable[/b]\n-The AI is not very consistent. Most of the time it plays pretty well, but sometimes enemy ships can get stuck or perform some obviously dumb actions\n\nOverall the game is very enjoyable, so get it, especially if you see it on sale.",
